cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Predictive Modelling of Social Media Trend Emergence:
  fusing temporal, sentiment and network-diffusion signals
message: >-
  This repository contains the code for a final-year undergraduate
  data science project. It is coursework, not a peer-reviewed
  publication. The underlying tweet corpus is not distributed here.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Saifullahshamsi"
    email: jawedh011@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Saifullahshamsi/Final_Year_Project"
abstract: >-
  An offline study predicting topic-level trend emergence on Twitter
  ahead of peak, on a static one-day historical corpus. Three feature
  channels normally studied in isolation — temporal volume dynamics,
  multilingual sentiment, and mention/reply interaction-graph structure
  — are fused, and each channel's marginal contribution is isolated by
  ablation. Evaluation uses PR-AUC as the headline metric under
  topic-grouped cross-validation, with a lead-time curve as the
  evidence for extended prediction horizon.
keywords:
  - trend prediction
  - social network analysis
  - information diffusion
  - signal fusion
  - Twitter
